A||||2||Greg Piet||What is the firewall gap?||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||01-24-2001||12:08 AM||||Behind the drivers seat what is the gap between the firewall(s)?<P>I know some of you audio folks put woofers in there, I just need to know how long of a bolt I need to make it through from behind the drivers seat to the engine compartment.  I have not drilled holes yet, and if the gap is too big I may find another solution to my idea.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-24-2001||10:00 AM||||The gap near the bottom is 2 1/2" deep. You do not want to drill a hole near the top of the gap as the gas tank filler tube passes thru. If you hit that you'll have a huge problem. If you are trying to drill a hole to run wires, you can go thru the center under the computer or drill a hole about 1.5" above the gap on the passenger side. This puts the hole over the top of the brake line and below the harness and battery box.<BR>Just let us know what you are doing with the hole and we'll let you know where to put it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||01-24-2001||11:01 AM||||Never mind.<BR>I have found another solution to my project.<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
